[[File:Basilisk Knight icon.png|left]]
'''Basilisk Knights''' are a [[Slayer]] creature that can be found in [[Jormungand's Prison]] beneath the [[Island of Stone]], requiring level 60 Slayer and completion of [[The Fremennik Exiles]] to kill. Like [[cockatrice]] and [[basilisk]]s, players must equip a [[mirror shield]] or [[V's shield]] when fighting these monsters or they will take heavy damage and their stats will be drained. Uniquely, the attack speed of Basilisk Knights will match the player's current attack speed if they are outside of melee range, but can only go as low as 4 ticks if the player is using a faster weapon, like [[throwing knives]].

The basilisk knight has an improved drop table from regular basilisks, and can drop the [[basilisk jaw]], which can be used to upgrade the [[Helm of Neitiznot]] to the [[Neitiznot faceguard]]. It should be noted that the basilisk jaw drops at an extremely low rate (1/5000) when not on a Basilisk Slayer task (purchased and unlocked via [[Slayer Rewards]]). Killing Basilisk Knights while on task grants a drop rate five times higher (1/1000) than killing them regularly.

Players cannot use a [[dwarf multicannon]] on Basilisk Knights, as the only places players can place a cannon in Jormungand's Prison are those which contain [[dagannoth]]. Additionally, players cannot resurrect [[thrall]]s in Jormungand's Prison.

While on a basilisk Slayer task, there is a 1/200 chance that a [[Basilisk Sentinel]] will spawn after you kill a Basilisk Knight (if you have [[Slayer Rewards|Bigger and Badder]] unlocked). After claiming the elite tier rewards from the [[Combat Achievements]] system, this chance is increased to 1/150.

